# Review ownership for CI and the scripts that drive a run.
#
# GitHub consults this file ONLY when it evaluates a pull request's reviews, and ONLY from the
# branch that pull request TARGETS -- never from the default branch. On its own it blocks
# nothing: what gives it force is whichever repository ruleset applies to THIS branch.
# A copy missing from one branch protects nothing there and fails SILENTLY, by requesting
# no review at all, which is why the file exists on each of the three long-lived branches
# (`dev`, `test`, `prod`) and is kept identical across them.
#
# There is no ruleset field for "CI or scripts", so the guarded set is exactly the paths
# listed here. A path absent from this list is a path any maintainer may change and merge
# alone. The list is deliberately broad — all of `/scripts/`, not a subdirectory of it —
# because a helper that provisions accounts or grants access is as load-bearing as CI.
#
# The cost is stated rather than discovered: an ordinary change to a helper script now
# waits on the code owner. If that owner cannot keep up, the honest fix is to narrow this
# list on purpose or add owners — not to bypass it, because a gate bypassed on every run
# is not a gate.

/.github/ @michaelmarshall
/scripts/ @michaelmarshall
